{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "מטה משפט", :translit "mateh mishpat", :gloss "perverting justice"} {:he "שהיודע הדין ומטהו בראיותיו", :translit "shehayodea hadin umetoho b'ra'otav", :gloss "who knows the law and perverts it with his proofs"} {:he "או טוען שקר הוא משגה עור", :translit "o to'en sheker hu masgeh iver", :gloss "or a fraudulent litigant, he misleads the blind"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Verse phrase מטה משפט read as double reference: corrupt judge and fraudulent litigant"}], :frame {:text "The phrase מטה משפט appears in the curse catalogue of Deuteronomy 27:19 alongside משגה עור בדרך. Rabbinic legal tradition treats perversion of justice as a primary category of judicial corruption: a judge who knows the correct law but distorts it through specious proofs (Sanhedrin 7b; Shabbat 10a). The same verse's language of misleading the blind is applied in rabbinic sources to anyone who gives bad counsel or causes another to stumble (Pe'ah 5:6; Sifrei Deuteronomy 282).", :sources ["Deuteronomy 27:19" "Sanhedrin 7b" "Shabbat 10a" "Pe'ah 5:6" "Sifrei Deuteronomy 282"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Verse phrase מטה משפט read as double reference: corrupt judge and fraudulent litigant", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:39:47.581079288Z", :model "glm-5.2"}